{"title":"UCI CX World Cup Debuts in Czechia with Ostrava’s Snow & Industrial Night Racing","link":"https://bikerumor.com/uci-cx-world-cup-debuts-in-czechia-with-ostravas-snow-industrial-night-racing/","date":1795797551000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Lilli-ODonnell-running-away-with-the-junior-women-victory-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"&lt;i&gt;(All photos/Cory Benson)&lt;/i&gt;\" /></p>\n<p>UCI World Cup cross racing kicks off this weekend with a Czech double-header – beginning in Ostrava.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>But this is a story more about the unique start the UCI Cyclo-Cross World Cup takes this season in Ostrava, CZ. Beacuse not only is this an all-new venue for the World Cup – itself pretty wild as it’s an old industrial site inside the city, but it’s also taking place at night… under a ton of flood lights. Oh, and a snowstorm dropped in yesterday, covering the racetrack in a blanket of snow, and creating near white-out conditions for the Junior Women &amp; Men racing last night!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>CX World Cup kicks off in Ostrava, CZ winter wasteland</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: does snow mean more work for team mechanics?\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_team-mechanic-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(All photos/Cory Benson)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Yeah, this is more a tale of iconic cyclocross vibes, rather than a new bike story, or even much about the first racing results of the opener. So, instead of my typical bike tech style of covering cross racing, I’m kicking it off with more of a gallery about racing in this old industrial Moravian wasteland, in the snow, and at night under the lights.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: USA Cycling team in the snow\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_winter-vibes-for-USA-Cycling-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The first World Cup of the season is always a test of the mechanics and team logistics. It’s often the first real global challenge. Adding a bunch of snow, made that all the more complex. Lucky for the mechanics, the course hasn’t gotten too muddy – the Ostrava course has a lot of paved surfaces hiding under that snow.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>So there weren’t a ton of bikes to constantly pressure wash. Instead, I spotted more action with mini electric air blasters blowing snow &amp; sand out of bike drivetrains, making sure melt water didn’t freeze up on the bikes.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>USA Cycling was just one of many digging through snow to keep their athletes going. And today ahead of the Elite races you were as likely to see mechanics shoveling snow-free places to work as you were to see them fixing bikes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Junior Women’s &amp; Junior Men’s first wins of the World Cup weekend</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: American Lilli O'Donnell crossed her heart for a dominant win\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_cross-your-heart-hope-to-win-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Officially, last night’s preview of Junior Women &amp; Junior Men wasn’t the World Cup. Save that for the U23 &amp; Elites racing tonight. But the racing was top-level, and the conditions were ideal for cross racers to show who was the strongest!</p>\n\n\n\n<p>One the women’s front, young American racer and Pan-Am champ Lilliana O’Donnell took the first win in a dominant fashion as the snow started to pick up. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1125\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: Junior Men winner Ondrej Bukovsky racnig in the snow\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-men-winner-Ondrej-Bukovsky-in-a-mid-race-snowstorm-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Then, you Czech rider Ondřej Bukovský did the same in the Junior Men’s field, riding out early and stayoing away in the heavy blowing snow.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>CX World Cup in the old Vítkovice ironworks in Ostrava, Czechia</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-1536x1024.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: old industrial site\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area-1350x900.jpg 1350w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_old-Vitkovice-industrial-area.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-1536x1024.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: racing in an old steel mill\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland-1350x900.jpg 1350w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_industrial-wasteland.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The backdrop of the Ostrava Cross World Cup is the old Vítkovice ironworks. So, while about 1/3 of the track looks like a classic Euro cyclocross course, winding up and down short, steep grassy hills and off-cambers, the rest is set in between a bunch of dark, decaying old industrial buildings.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"922\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-1536x922.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: winter wonderland racing under the lights\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland-1500x900.jpg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_racing-in-a-winter-wonderland.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"864\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-1536x864.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: I don't even know what this is?\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights-1600x900.jpg 1600w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_skull-lights.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>But the ironworks is also a historically protected site, so it’s still quite a popular spot for visitors as well. There are a number of reinovated building turned into museums, restaurants, cafes, and hotels on-site. And there’s a big outdoor LED light art exhibit that the racers meander through, making the industrial wasteland somehow look like a festive winter wonderland under the falling snow!</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s a pretty wild juxtaposition. </p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Back to the racing…</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-1536x1024.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: not much snow at the start\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow-1350x900.jpg 1350w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_training-before-the-heaviest-snow.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"922\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-1536x922.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: less mud, more slush\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush-1500x900.jpg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_not-much-mud-but-plenty-of-slush.jpg 2000w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>With a strange backdrop, the athletes are tackling something completely new to most. Then, throw a bunch of fresh snow and ever-changing ruts into the mix and it’s anyone’s guess how the Elite racing will turn out.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: snowy chaos in deep sand\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juinor-men-chaos-in-sand-and-snow-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>One thing is for sure – chaos.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>A big sandy descent covered with snow, but not quite frozen should keep things interesting on Friday night.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: racing in a heavy snowstorm\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_junior-womens-racing-in-heavy-snowstorm-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>As far as I can remember, I don’t think the Cyclo-Cross World Cup has ever had a night race. And a few Elite racers have noted that alone will shake up the bunch. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: Junior Men winner Ondrej Bukovsky in the sandy, snowy descent\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-descending-in-snd-and-snow-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>There’s still forecast to be a few flurries coming down for the Elite Women &amp; Men, but at least they won’t have to deal with the heavy snow the Juniors saw.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava: Junior Men winner Ondrej Bukovsky\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Ondrej-Bukovsky-junior-men-winner-finish-line-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>That should make it a bit easier for fans to follow along at home. You know, being able to see the riders when the cameras zoom down the long straights.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow.jpg\" alt=\"CX World Cup Ostrava in a near whiteout snowstorm\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/CX-World-Cup-Ostrava-preview_Juniors-racing-in-the-snow-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>When I popped out the zoom lens to follow the Junior Men’s leader late in the race, pretty much all I could see were snowflakes, backlit by the flood lights.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>We’ll see if visibility is higher tonight!</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.ucicyclocrossworldcup.com/en\" target=\"_blank\">UCICyclo-CrossWorldCup.com</a></em></p>","author":"Cory Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/uci-cx-world-cup-debuts-in-czechia-with-ostravas-snow-industrial-night-racing/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"5ee37ab46d771d23f8ec91223485a335721b5baa361cfb79ae2c87dbe01e1ce4","category":"Cycling"}